For each word below, write ONE short sentence (12 to 22 words) that uses the word itself, spelled in full, in the sense given. Give it voice and mood: a question, someone speaking, a sigh, delight, a warning. No definitions; show the word in a moment of life. Answer as one JSON object mapping each WORD (as given, upper case) to its sentence. JSON only.

ACCORD: harmony of people's opinions or actions or characters.
ADD: a condition (mostly in boys) characterized by behavioral and learning disorders.
AGAINST: Abreast.
AGENT: an active and efficient cause.
ALIGN: place in a line or arrange so as to be parallel or straight.
ALPHA: the 1st letter of the Greek alphabet.
APPEND: add to the very end.
ARCHIVE: a depository containing historical records and documents.
ARRAY: an orderly arrangement.
ASSET: a useful or valuable quality.
ATOM: (physics and chemistry) the smallest component of an element having the chemical properties of the element.
CAPABILITY: the quality of being capable -- physically or intellectually or legally.
